  <section class="ahome__block read" aria-labelledby="read">
    <h2 id="read">Firms without year marks</h2>
    <p>Neither Rainwater’s <cite>Encyclopedia of American Silver Manufacturers</cite> nor Kovels’ dictionary of marks gives year marks for Towle, Wallace, Kirk, Durgin or Dominick &amp; Haff. Silver by those firms is dated by changes in its trademark and by its pattern.</p>
    <p>Gorham’s year marks have their own page: <a href="/marks/gorham-silver-marks">Gorham silver marks</a>.</p>
    <p>The pictures here are cut from Rainwater’s encyclopedia, a book still in copyright, and shown for reference with its page.</p>
  </section>
  <AppBox text="Photograph the marks. The Advisor reads the trademark and the year mark together and keeps the reading with the photo." />
